WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Motor neurons carry messages
that help us move.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Branching dendrites receive input.
The cell body supports the neuron.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.000
An electrical signal travels
along the axon.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:21.000
At the nerve–muscle junction, chemical
messengers help activate a muscle fiber.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:26.000
In ALS, motor neurons degenerate and
connections to muscle can be lost.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Less nerve supply contributes to weakness.
The pattern and pace vary for each person.
